  "enhanced_information": "Deprenyl is used in the treatment of Parkinson's disease as a suicide inhibitor of the MAO-B enzyme, leading to increased dopamine levels by preventing dopamine breakdown. It does not directly affect dopamine receptors or act as a dopamine D2 receptor agonist. It also inhibits COMT, increasing dopamine availability and improving motor symptoms in Parkinson's disease."
